    "why": "One strict index per entity, as the canonical JSON of what creates it. Every column is typed - the neutral type in `meta.sde_type` where the native type alone would not say how to read the value back - the key keeps its declared order in `_meta.sde.key`, and each text field, but not the uuid one, has a token field beside it under `__sde_tokens`. The relation's column is a plain keyword: every mapped field is indexed, so there is no index for a layout to declare."
